// src/v4/compiler/05_eval.dag
//
// Scope: evaluator/interpreter — directly executes an InferredTree without emitting target source. THE PRIMARY execution path (THESIS:225 "dag run is the primary execution path"). Sibling of 05_emit.dag: both consume InferredTree; eval EXECUTES, emit PROJECTS to target languages (omni-emission). eval is primary; emit is the projection.
// Anchor: THESIS:225 (dag run primary execution path) + https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interpreter_(computing) + concept-unification THESIS:188 (interpreter runtime = language spec = transport spec)
// Primary: per THESIS:225 eval is the DEFAULT execution path; emit is
//   the omni-emission projection. Same InferredTree input as 05_emit.dag
//   (concept-unification: interpreter runtime = language spec = transport
//   spec, THESIS:188). NOT stage 6 — parallel backend to emit at stage 5.
//
// Owns:
//   - eval: (InferredTree, Inputs) -> Result<Value, Diagnostic>
//   - bounded execution (INVARIANTS P4 decidability — no unbounded loops)
//   - THE runner that three things compose over:
//     - workflow/bootstrap.dag (interpreted, not compiled — v2's eval
//       seeds, then v4's own eval)
//     - TestClaim evaluation (run the claim, check the assertion)
//     - lens dry-run / structural-execution-trace (eval without effects)
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag, std/diagnostic.dag, std/witness.dag
//   - compiler/04_infer.dag: InferredTree (shared with 05_emit.dag)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-22
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).

module v4.compiler.eval

